#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119650 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1d809050-9477-5de6-8c95-7294804e7b69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4943" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119651 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "c1576b30-9142-5884-b654-7ade7a765ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4944" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119652 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f952e670-a673-5c15-913b-c396e8885142" :question/math-academy-id "e-4945" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](images/64/64a3661b0699fbde542ed1709bacf569f681477a5f824f0650b07d9060b82dae.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01df1bcb-4a7b-5150-ad54-aeccce8f3856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399610} {:answer/id #uuid "38c936a1-d976-513a-81ce-1b234231b7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399611} {:answer/id #uuid "039d4336-0a52-5143-9cf6-0afb00570546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,7,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399612} {:answer/id #uuid "663befe7-68ee-5370-a09d-addae6ba4a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399613} {:answer/id #uuid "012c8472-6cf0-52d5-b45e-45eeef9775df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01df1bcb-4a7b-5150-ad54-aeccce8f3856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399610} :answer-field/id #uuid "44bd467d-d957-573d-927f-7c7473314928" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "310a805e-d3a4-5eae-9540-0ee13a3dc212" :question/math-academy-id "q-108309" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,-1⟩+t⟨-1,2,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩=11.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ -2(2-t)+1(3+2t)+4(-1+3t) & =11 \\\\ -4+2t+3+2t-4+12t & =11 \\\\ 16t & =16 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-1,3+2(1),-1+3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,5,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10f49541-bf17-51d7-9f75-37616f1a6089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475468} {:answer/id #uuid "60c57a2e-889c-5474-81d3-a55d65fdd34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475585} {:answer/id #uuid "813ea0c8-6a02-5346-b587-75a643aadca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475635} {:answer/id #uuid "b4214275-5327-55f6-a028-7523f95b454a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475710} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf64d63-9b14-5d35-91c0-7a22161af6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbf64d63-9b14-5d35-91c0-7a22161af6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475730} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cedb4ab-8127-56c0-a22d-80bf5a1ac4a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ef5750d-a5da-50af-8419-8b1661dfe47b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108319" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-2⟩+t⟨3,-1,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩=8.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5+3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5+3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩ & =8 \\\\ ⟨5-3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩ & =8 \\\\ -2(5+3t)+4(3-t)+5\\cdot (-2+2t) & =8 \\\\ -10-6t+12-4t-10+10t & =8 \\\\ -8 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cbd933f-3f29-5070-8231-31ef77e6f4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(20,29,40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399631} {:answer/id #uuid "f073d53a-a8e7-5ae2-82c8-e5cb31403d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-23,-25)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399632} {:answer/id #uuid "654434c9-d7c4-5e1e-bfe8-aaafc9425c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-7,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399633} {:answer/id #uuid "509a688f-9e49-51a5-95ba-17bf03e47002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399634} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ec3fa5-fe3a-5ef1-bb6e-18d2712b8636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,9,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1ec3fa5-fe3a-5ef1-bb6e-18d2712b8636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,9,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399635} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4bd1c19-a96b-51b8-b83f-2c4bebba5b26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ee9813a-b1b3-5ef0-86f7-ac30b2000775" :question/math-academy-id "q-108368" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2t \\\\ y=-3+4t \\\\ z=5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+2y-z=33.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z & =33 \\\\ 3(4+2t)+2(-3+4t)-(5t) & =33 \\\\ 12+6t-6+8t-5t & =33 \\\\ 9t & =27 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2(3)=10 \\\\ y=-3+4(3)=9 \\\\ z=5(3)=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(10,9,15).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007d69dc-a2ca-580f-b0f7-74cbcfa1ebdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475444} {:answer/id #uuid "3a25e529-3954-5987-92eb-d533381cc44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,31,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475523} {:answer/id #uuid "52af092c-e727-5f18-8ff7-345347fe6d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-13,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475562} {:answer/id #uuid "572842f6-cb5d-5a22-b2c9-50266f22eb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475570} {:answer/id #uuid "fca47535-789f-5b0b-98b2-271a04ca1b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-14,-21,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a25e529-3954-5987-92eb-d533381cc44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,31,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475523} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8937436-576e-5320-a137-6b981c96167e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "07e33caa-9650-5834-8d9a-46cc82f723d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-108434" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+s⟨1,0,2⟩+t⟨0,-2,3⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,2⟩\\times ⟨0,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =4i-3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨4,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =⟨5,3,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+3w,-1+4w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ 4(1+3w)-3(-1+4w)-2(2-w) & =19 \\\\ 4+12w+3-12w-4+2w & =19 \\\\ 2w & =16 \\\\ w & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=8$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1+3(8),-1+4(8),2-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨25,31,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(25,31,-6).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a4e4e53-6530-5d9b-ac71-88fa4a852643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,5,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514894} {:answer/id #uuid "13d7977a-6ece-5a3d-a4d3-a046ae5ee70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,3,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514914} {:answer/id #uuid "3e792c4b-0f89-58e4-ad54-bf65b7f20967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515006} {:answer/id #uuid "97dcbf66-8c48-507d-96c6-a848577b2e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-3,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515192} {:answer/id #uuid "a9993b57-a418-5d19-be94-6b1c3a3b00c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,5,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13d7977a-6ece-5a3d-a4d3-a046ae5ee70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,3,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514914} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d9ffbc-23ef-519d-9512-884d3bb1903d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "83aacc67-1785-59c3-94ae-6f65bea01fe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-108881" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y+1}{2}=\\frac{z}{4},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩=25.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,-1,0)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,2,4⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,-1,0⟩+t⟨3,2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =25 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =25 \\\\ 3(-2+3t)-(-1+2t)+2(4t) & =25 \\\\ -6+9t+1-2t+8t & =25 \\\\ 15t & =30 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(2),-1+2(2),4(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,3,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(4,3,8).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399650 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c181d54f-7b5e-5e40-b660-5db606239a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,7,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399652} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2c2f01-60e6-5197-ae47-76dd272575a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399653} {:answer/id #uuid "100fc206-faa0-5c9a-8c1d-f828c27459ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399654} {:answer/id #uuid "a03ac96b-8e87-5579-959e-6059ecf3486c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399655} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d8eeca-91ef-5d44-a9a1-da7d1707ffce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "100fc206-faa0-5c9a-8c1d-f828c27459ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399654} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd4a0b3-55ce-54d3-98c8-8b7021d46e30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d225520-d7e9-5a28-afbf-6e16563a3611" :question/math-academy-id "q-108889" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩=39.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(3,1,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨5,2,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨3,1,-4⟩+t⟨5,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ (-3)(3+5t)+2(1+2t)-(-4+3t) & =39 \\\\ -9-15t+2+4t+4-3t & =39 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-3),1+2(-3),-4+3(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,-5,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(-12,-5,-13).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35e34ef5-0c0f-566b-94a8-9376d485a3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475516} {:answer/id #uuid "384678c4-4350-5113-9f0f-32d8e2cf6110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475518} {:answer/id #uuid "92098877-886b-53fa-a483-755c30d71d2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475660} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c22028-564a-5c89-ab16-c9763fcf688a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475706} {:answer/id #uuid "c36ccfc7-634d-5201-b479-3d9288da2e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2c22028-564a-5c89-ab16-c9763fcf688a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475706} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d0e6f8-2892-55f4-a237-affcef970729" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e4fbd5e6-b819-591a-880c-a933bdaba9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-33082" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,1⟩+w⟨-3,-2,3⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-15,1,1⟩+s⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨1,4,0⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩\\times ⟨1,4,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-8i+2j+8k \\\\  & =⟨-8,2,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =⟨-15,1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2,3,1⟩+w⟨-3,-2,3⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130 \\\\ ⟨2-3w,3-2w,1+3w⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130 \\\\ -8(2-3w)+2(3-2w)+8(1+3w) & =130 \\\\ -16+24w+6-4w+8+24w & =130 \\\\ 44w & =132 \\\\ w & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨2-3(3),3-2(3),1+3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,-3,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-7,-3,10).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01d22185-31e1-5c2b-95d2-848598ea1898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302463} {:answer/id #uuid "60c4e451-1a44-53d9-a6db-f9fb648545be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303045} {:answer/id #uuid "67e0400e-fa7a-57ba-96e7-b214d9574656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-5,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303086} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d1ed36-c9fa-51a0-96ce-45e0b3571939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303488} {:answer/id #uuid "dcb202fe-418e-5930-8986-b2659604d5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d1ed36-c9fa-51a0-96ce-45e0b3571939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303488} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dc757d8-b74c-5e82-84ca-760fef027983" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c9e4b1e-64e1-5274-81d9-5dc1e69f7cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-33194" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,1,0⟩+t⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,Π:3x-2y+4z+6=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+4z & =-6 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ ⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ 3(2+t)-2(1+3t)+4(2t) & =-6 \\\\ 6+3t-2-6t+8t & =-6 \\\\ 5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(-2),1+3(-2),2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(0,-5,-4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb8f532-8109-56ef-8ea6-7d7e8fda174e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,31,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312080} {:answer/id #uuid "30de8d47-2f26-5381-bc67-4eb0ee992123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,13,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312369} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f8512a-48d0-5872-a500-e1de657bfe34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,13,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313291} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b9d8a5-8b12-541b-b956-720a78e83b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313762} {:answer/id #uuid "f5cde894-634d-5f97-9e4d-09a5ae155357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,-20,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30de8d47-2f26-5381-bc67-4eb0ee992123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,13,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312369} :answer-field/id #uuid "85681f3e-c4a0-5f09-ab05-6853a3e1d4ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f60e171f-8d34-5a7f-bcb5-85d2254301da" :question/math-academy-id "q-33988" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+t⟨-5,2,7⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩=30.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ ⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ 2(5-5t)+3(3+2t)-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 10-10t+9+6t-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 3t & =15 \\\\ t & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5-5(5),3+2(5),-4+7(5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-20,13,31⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-20,13,31).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a523b91-b0c8-5d77-ac05-a918d500094c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312052} {:answer/id #uuid "82d8d2f3-12d7-5f69-9c67-b4d2db7dc5da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313028} {:answer/id #uuid "8d14825a-42af-51a3-9f03-b6163ac5f748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313102} {:answer/id #uuid "95ed7638-8aa8-5f1b-b639-82099d0d033c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,7,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313173} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ba162d-d3e7-561c-ba10-731b0f92f98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5ba162d-d3e7-561c-ba10-731b0f92f98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313525} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d7ba987-d1b7-522f-859e-b04e23ff46bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c755ffbb-8374-5c52-a967-a6387ef6da9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-33992" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=-3-5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-5y+3z-84=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+3z-84 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-5(-1+4t)+3(-3-5t) & =84 \\\\ 10-4t+5-20t-9-15t & =84 \\\\ -39t & =78 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-2)=9 \\\\ y=-1+4(-2)=-9 \\\\ z=-3-5(-2)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(9,-9,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2280cb71-d56d-5c11-9ffc-9e7ac8621681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-17,-10,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339424} {:answer/id #uuid "51d70f39-09be-5fe0-b06a-f48d5b7f85d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339879} {:answer/id #uuid "7923bb17-a47c-5f0f-aa70-02c9163dfd5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-13,-10,17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340209} {:answer/id #uuid "a3365d47-2432-5573-a0bc-2a03360f17ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340608} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6d6aad-b4fa-596f-8dd5-f5bc35997084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-10,-13,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7923bb17-a47c-5f0f-aa70-02c9163dfd5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-13,-10,17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340209} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ab4e761-07dd-58e8-b46a-0567acd50ed3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7b7455d-19c2-5862-8ffa-6bf81d08e53f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73985" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨3,2,-3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩=6.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ ⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ 5(2+3t)-2(2t)+3(2-3t) & =6 \\\\ 10+15t-4t+6-9t & =6 \\\\ 2t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+3(-5),2(-5),2-3(-5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-10,17⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-13,-10,17).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a8eacf-acaa-535b-84fd-68dd0e55e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-3,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339449} {:answer/id #uuid "9245627b-7ed9-5a81-a591-0bddaf5c1488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340440} {:answer/id #uuid "95647350-28b0-50f0-ba88-074ca618981c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340476} {:answer/id #uuid "a8076978-e0f4-543d-834d-5fa159290d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340652} {:answer/id #uuid "cce78ef0-b9c9-5c65-96ff-bcf9b11be57b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8076978-e0f4-543d-834d-5fa159290d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340652} :answer-field/id #uuid "75a90e21-4110-5920-b29a-9528326a3c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a27e98ee-3a96-559d-b75b-2bf4d0ce11d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-73987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨5,2,-4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=36.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ ⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ 2(1+5t)-3(1+2t)+5(1-4t) & =36 \\\\ 2+10t-3-6t+5-20t & =36 \\\\ -16t & =32 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+5(-2),1+2(-2),1-4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,-3,9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-9,-3,9).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fc86f8-0368-54eb-a3e0-3cf6b0379332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-16,-16,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483621} {:answer/id #uuid "2143e54b-67d5-5002-957a-3bf88c230ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(24,-11,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483624} {:answer/id #uuid "257b548a-b52d-5b2d-8a2f-57d74b50d39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483630} {:answer/id #uuid "7944f3e7-3b31-5e5a-b5cb-a1562208eb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-13,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483813} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a4f2b9-c6e0-5e67-8ab6-66d592472d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(26,12,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20fc86f8-0368-54eb-a3e0-3cf6b0379332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-16,-16,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483621} :answer-field/id #uuid "15f90597-4c03-5ae4-b2c2-f42eae091087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12b4f5c6-720f-5c2c-b1e8-295eb7dcb29c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73991" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-2t \\\\ y=5-3t \\\\ z=-1+2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x-2y+6z=62.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+6z & =62 \\\\ 3(-2-2t)-2(5-3t)+6(-1+2t) & =62 \\\\ -6-6t-10+6t-6+12t & =62 \\\\ 12t & =84 \\\\ t & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=6$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-2(7)=-16 \\\\ y=5-3(7)=-16 \\\\ z=-1+2(7)=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-16,-16,13).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b2ccf68-fbc4-58ea-80f0-c47a1f4e61c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339365} {:answer/id #uuid "1d364631-26c0-59a4-93c9-0842ba8027a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(19,10,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339381} {:answer/id #uuid "2bfe2f6a-4b05-5041-9be9-ec95d41ced84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,8,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339510} {:answer/id #uuid "90fc5ea2-94e0-5824-91af-e274368bde07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,11,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340429} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f82de1-4dec-5d15-9285-344580d1aa1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90fc5ea2-94e0-5824-91af-e274368bde07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,11,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340429} :answer-field/id #uuid "3769c405-5ffb-59ea-8180-d6fbf6837b56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a17e320-306c-50fa-b84b-f8cbe958e629" :question/math-academy-id "q-73993" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=-2-6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x-2y+4z-132=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y+4z-132 & =0 \\\\ 5(3-5t)-2(2-3t)+4(-2-6t) & =132 \\\\ 15-25t-4+6t-8-24t & =132 \\\\ -43t & =129 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5(-3)=18 \\\\ y=2-3(-3)=11 \\\\ z=-2-6(-3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(18,11,16).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5220f57b-422e-531b-842b-1f584644f261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339883} {:answer/id #uuid "979f8148-7b8d-5ec3-a55e-fb37aea141d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340493} {:answer/id #uuid "b83d885e-e879-51ab-96e4-b43985498ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340786} {:answer/id #uuid "bb602b66-8066-5891-8e86-1da45546964a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340805} {:answer/id #uuid "bba3c359-7475-5f71-8622-34809c6c9b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,21,-14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb602b66-8066-5891-8e86-1da45546964a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340805} :answer-field/id #uuid "10fba32d-90d3-5858-a355-57f3ffefce29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d4d8f0f-1eab-5bd0-8f71-a26637e6257d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74003" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$"}]}
